OL,3,GNEWSATheft-accused trio 'made friends'
OL,4,Awith King's lambs
OL,5,
OL,6,FThree animal rights protesters accused
OL,7,Fof stealing lambs owned by King Charles
OL,8,Fspent several hours in a field so they
OL,9,Fcould "make friends" with the sheep
OL,10,Fbefore taking them, a court has heard.
OL,12,FOn the second day of a trial at Norwich
OL,13,FCrown Court, the Animal Rising
OL,14,Factivists described how they "rescued"
OL,15,Fthree lambs from a farm on the
OL,16,FSandringham Estate in Norfolk in May
OL,17,F2023.
OL,19,FRose Sharkey, 26, Rose Patterson, 37
OL,20,Fand Sarah Foy, 26, all deny a charge of
OL,21,Ftheft but admit taking the lambs to
OL,22,F"save them from harm".
OL,23,APub: 23-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
